  m_Name: Blade21
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade (6)
  description: The Blade (6) is a key component of the jet engine's compressor section,
    where it compresses the air and directs it into the combustion chamber. Its position
    and shape are carefully designed to minimize energy losses and maximize airflow,
    making it an essential component of the engine's efficiency. Notably, the Blade
    (6) is often made from a high-strength, lightweight material, such as aluminum
    or titanium alloy, to reduce the engine's overall weight and increase its power-to-weight
    ratio.
